cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite the version and profile actually used. RadAccord 1.3.0rc1 is a research release candidate with explicit CT quantization and observation before native MIRP feature calculation. Earlier scientific phases remain separately archived."
title: "RadAccord: software for physical consistency testing before radiomic feature reuse in research"
type: software
version: 1.3.0rc1
date-released: 2026-09-09
authors:
  - family-names: García-Hidalgo
    given-names: Clemente
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-6672-2714"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: "Research software compares declared physical processing with observed image and ROI states in supported radiomics workflows. Native PyRadiomics and MIRP integrations preserve requested feature values while reporting bounded evidence; feature formulae, unobserved states and clinical validity are outside the assessment. Earlier sampling and full-grid/scalar studies are retained separately from the evolving native integration profiles."
repository-code: "https://github.com/torkitor/RadAccord"
url: "https://github.com/torkitor/RadAccord"
keywords:
  - radiomics
  - medical imaging
  - physical consistency
  - reproducibility
  - scientific software
